╭─ VULN-0006 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: Verbose Error Pages Expose Stack Traces and Internal Application     │
│  Paths                                                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: MEDIUM                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 5.3                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://juiceshop:3000                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /redirect, /ftp/suspicious_errors.yml, /rest/products             │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: GET                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  The application returns verbose HTML error pages containing full stack      │
│  traces to unauthenticated users. These error responses disclose internal    │
│  filesystem paths, source filenames and line numbers, and framework/library  │
│  versions.                                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  This behavior was confirmed across multiple endpoints and HTTP status       │
│  codes (403/406/500). The disclosed implementation details materially        │
│  increase attacker effectiveness by enabling precise technology              │
│  fingerprinting and targeted exploit development.                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  Unauthenticated attackers can retrieve detailed internal implementation     │
│  information, including absolute internal paths (e.g.,                       │
│  “/juice-shop/build/routes/...”), library versions (e.g., Express), and      │
│  code locations (file names and line numbers). This accelerates              │
│  exploitation by:                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Enabling targeted attacks against known-vulnerable components/versions.     │
│  Improving the reliability of endpoint discovery and bypass techniques.      │
│  Supporting chaining with other vulnerabilities (e.g., SQL injection/auth    │
│  bypass) by revealing internal routing and middleware behavior.              │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The application’s error handling returns a developer-oriented HTML error    │
│  page rather than a generic error response. The responses include a          │
│  “stacktrace” section that contains:                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Internal filesystem paths (e.g., “/juice-shop/build/...”,                   │
│  “/juice-shop/node_modules/...”).                                            │
│  Source file names and line/column numbers (e.g., “redirect.js:45:18”,       │
│  “insecurity.js:149:34”).                                                    │
│  Framework version disclosure (e.g., “OWASP Juice Shop (Express ^4.21.0)”).  │
│                                                                              │
│  Confirmed examples:                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  GET /redirect?to=https://example.com returns HTTP 406 and includes a full   │
│  stack trace showing “/juice-shop/build/routes/redirect.js:45:18” and        │
│  Express router internals (evidence ref: 2914).                              │
│                                                                              │
│  GET /redirect (missing required parameter) returns HTTP 500 and includes    │
│  stack frames such as “/juice-shop/build/lib/insecurity.js:149:34” and       │
│  “/juice-shop/build/routes/redirect.js:38:22” (evidence ref: 3082).          │
│                                                                              │
│  GET /ftp/suspicious_errors.yml returns HTTP 403 with an error page that     │
│  includes a stack trace revealing                                            │
│  “/juice-shop/build/routes/fileServer.js:59:18” and                          │
│  “/juice-shop/node_modules/serve-index/index.js:145:39” (evidence ref:       │
│  717).                                                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  GET /rest/products returns HTTP 500 and includes stack frames such as       │
│  “/juice-shop/build/routes/angular.js:42:18” and Express router internals    │
│  (evidence ref: 3085).                                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  This indicates misconfigured production error handling (debug-style error   │
│  pages), where stack traces are rendered directly into responses.            │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Send an unauthenticated request to the redirect endpoint with a          │
│  disallowed target:                                                          │
│     GET http://juiceshop:3000/redirect?to=https://example.com                │
│     Expected: HTTP 406 with an HTML page containing “Express” and a          │
│  “stacktrace” list including internal paths.                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  2. Trigger an unhandled exception by omitting the required redirect         │
│  parameter:                                                                  │
│     GET http://juiceshop:3000/redirect                                       │
│     Expected: HTTP 500 with an HTML page containing “TypeError” and stack    │
│  frames including internal paths and source line numbers.                    │
│                                                                              │
│  3. Trigger an error page from file serving validation:                      │
│     GET http://juiceshop:3000/ftp/suspicious_errors.yml                      │
│     Expected: HTTP 403 with an HTML page containing “Only .md and .pdf       │
│  files are allowed!” plus a stack trace showing internal paths.              │
│                                                                              │
│  4. Trigger an “Unexpected path” error:                                      │
│     GET http://juiceshop:3000/rest/products                                  │
│     Expected: HTTP 500 with an HTML page containing “Unexpected path” and    │
│  stack trace showing internal paths and line numbers.                        │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import re                                                                   │
│  import sys                                                                  │
│  import requests                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  BASE = "http://juiceshop:3000"                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  TESTS = [                                                                   │
│      ("/redirect?to=https://example.com", 406),                              │
