╭─ VULN-0010 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: IDOR/BOLA Allows Cross-User Basket Read and BasketItem Modification  │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: HIGH                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 7.1                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://juiceshop:3000                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /rest/basket/{basketId}, /api/BasketItems/{id}                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: GET, PUT, POST                                                      │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:N                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  An Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) / Broken Object Level            │
│  Authorization (BOLA) vulnerability was identified in the shopping basket    │
│  functionality. By modifying numeric object identifiers in requests, an      │
│  authenticated low-privilege user can access and manipulate another user’s   │
│  basket and basket items.                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  The issue affects both a REST endpoint that returns basket contents by      │
│  basket ID and an API endpoint that allows direct read/update of basket      │
│  items by item ID. Authorization is not enforced to ensure the requested     │
│  basket or basket item belongs to the authenticated user.                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  An attacker with a standard customer account can perform unauthorized       │
│  actions against other customers’ shopping carts, including:                 │
│                                                                              │
│  Unauthorized read:                                                          │
│  Access another user’s basket metadata and contents (product list,           │
│  quantities), which may reveal purchasing intent and account activity.       │
│                                                                              │
│  Unauthorized modification:                                                  │
│  Modify another user’s basket items (e.g., change quantities), which can     │
│  disrupt purchases, cause fraudulent/unwanted orders, and create integrity   │
│  issues in commerce workflows.                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Business impact includes customer trust loss, increased support burden,     │
│  and potential financial fraud depending on downstream checkout/order        │
│  behavior.                                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The application exposes direct object references without enforcing          │
│  ownership checks:                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Affected endpoints:                                                         │
│  `GET /rest/basket/{basketId}`                                               │
│  Returns a basket object that includes a `UserId` field and embedded         │
│  `Products[]` entries. The server does not verify that `{basketId}` belongs  │
│  to the authenticated user.                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  `GET /api/BasketItems/{id}` and `PUT /api/BasketItems/{id}`                 │
│  Allow direct access to basket-item records by numeric ID and permit         │
│  updates (e.g., `quantity`) without verifying the basket item belongs to     │
│  the authenticated user’s basket.                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Validated evidence (proxy request IDs):                                     │
│  Owner basket read:                                                          │
│  Request `3224` returned basket `id:14` with `UserId:38` and included        │
│  `BasketItem id:13 quantity:1`.                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  Non-owner basket read:                                                      │
│  Request `3225` (performed as a different authenticated user) returned the   │
│  same basket `id:14` and `UserId:38`, demonstrating unauthorized cross-user  │
│  access.                                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│  Non-owner basket item read:                                                 │
│  Request `3226` returned basket item `id:13` with `BasketId:14 quantity:1`.  │
│                                                                              │
│  Non-owner basket item update:                                               │
│  Request `3227` updated basket item `id:13` to `quantity:4` while keeping    │
│  `BasketId:14`.                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  Owner verification:                                                         │
│  Request `3228` (owner reading `/rest/basket/14`) showed the basket item     │
│  quantity changed to `4`, confirming the unauthorized modification had       │
│  effect for the victim.                                                      │
│                                                                              │
│  Cleanup:                                                                    │
│  Request `3229` reverted quantity back to `1`, and request `3230` confirmed  │
│  the final basket view reflects quantity `1` again.                          │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Create two standard customer accounts (User A and User B) via `POST      │
│  /api/Users/`.                                                               │
│  2. Login as both users via `POST /rest/user/login` to obtain JWTs and each  │
│  user’s `bid` (basket ID).                                                   │
│  3. As User B (owner), create a basket item in their basket via `POST        │
│  /api/BasketItems/` and note the returned basket item ID.                    │
│  4. As User A (non-owner), request User B’s basket by ID:                    │
│     - `GET /rest/basket/{bid_of_userB}`                                      │
│     - Observe the response includes `UserId` belonging to User B and the     │
│  basket contents.                                                            │
│  5. As User A (non-owner), read and modify User B’s basket item by ID:       │
│     - `GET /api/BasketItems/{basketItemId}`                                  │
│     - `PUT /api/BasketItems/{basketItemId}` with `{"quantity":4}`            │
│  6. As User B (owner), verify their basket shows the modified quantity:      │
│     - `GET /rest/basket/{bid_of_userB}`                                      │
│  7. Revert changes (cleanup) as User B by setting the quantity back to the   │
│  original value.                                                             │
│                                                                              │
