╭─ VULN-0014 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: DOM-Based XSS in /#/search via Unsanitized q Parameter in            │
│  location.hash                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: CRITICAL                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 9.6                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://juiceshop:3000                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /#/search                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: GET                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:L                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  A DOM-based cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability was identified in the  │
│  Juice Shop client-side search route. The application reads the `q`          │
│  parameter from `location.hash` (e.g., `/#/search?q=...`), decodes it, and   │
│  renders it into the DOM as HTML without proper output                       │
│  encoding/sanitization.                                                      │
│                                                                              │
│  Because the injection occurs entirely in the browser, the server may not    │
│  observe the malicious payload in typical request logs. Any victim who       │
│  visits a crafted URL will execute attacker-controlled JavaScript in the     │
│  context of `http://juiceshop:3000`.                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  An attacker can execute arbitrary JavaScript in victims’ sessions,          │
│  enabling account takeover and unauthorized actions. During validation, the  │
│  application’s authentication token (JWT) was confirmed to be accessible to  │
│  injected JavaScript via both `document.cookie` and `localStorage`.          │
│                                                                              │
│  Practical impacts include:                                                  │
│  - Theft of JWT/session token leading to full account takeover               │
│  - Performing authenticated actions as the victim (e.g., purchases, profile  │
│  changes)                                                                    │
│  - Exfiltration of sensitive data accessible to the victim via same-origin   │
│  requests                                                                    │
│  - Potential privilege escalation if an administrator visits a crafted link  │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The vulnerable behavior occurs in the SPA route `/#/search`, where the      │
│  value of `q` is sourced from `location.hash` and inserted into the DOM in   │
│  an HTML-interpreted context (e.g., an `innerHTML`-equivalent sink). No      │
│  effective contextual output encoding is applied before rendering, allowing  │
│  an attacker to inject elements containing event handlers (e.g., `<img       │
│  onerror=...>`), resulting in script execution.                              │
│                                                                              │
│  Defense-in-depth controls were also observed to be insufficient for this    │
│  sink:                                                                       │
│  - No effective CSP was present to prevent inline event handler execution.   │
│  - The application stores the JWT in JavaScript-accessible storage           │
│  (`localStorage`) and in a cookie, making token theft straightforward once   │
│  XSS is achieved.                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Open the following URL in a browser:                                     │
│     `http://juiceshop:3000/#/search?q=%3Cimg%20src%3Dx%20onerror%3Dconsole.  │
│  log(1337)%3E`                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  2. Observe JavaScript execution:                                            │
│     - The browser console will log `1337`.                                   │
│     - DOM proof can be obtained by running:                                  │
│       - `document.querySelector('img[src="x"][onerror]').outerHTML`          │
│       - Expected output includes: `<img src="x"                              │
│  onerror="console.log(1337)">`                                               │
│                                                                              │
